\begin{document}
\section*{Kakeya Conjecture in Dimensions Four and Higher}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Four-dimensional Kakeya sets}: The manuscript claims that a set in $\mathbb R^4$ containing a segment of length one in every direction has Hausdorff dimension four. It permits arbitrary sets and arbitrary choices of witnessing segments.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} If $K\subset\mathbb R^4$ and for each unit direction $e\in S^3$ some $a_e\in\mathbb R^4$ satisfies $\{a_e+te:0\le t\le1\}\subset K$, then $\dim_H K=4$. No measurability assumption on $K$ or regularity assumption on the choice $e\mapsto a_e$ is imposed. This theorem treats dimension four, rather than all higher dimensions.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Four-dimensional Kakeya sets}: A hypothetical dimension loss is converted into a weighted incidence model for lines. Nested boxes and quadratic fits describe persistent concentration; each fit must retain enough incidence mass to contribute. Scalar comparison and planar rigidity then contradict the simultaneous density and time-length requirements forced on substantial terminal chart systems.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Four-dimensional Kakeya sets}: The manuscript’s result proves the Hausdorff dimension claim for n=4; the question higher-dimensional assertion also quantifies over all n>=5.

This page records partial support. Complete resolution of the catalogue question is not established by this record.

\subsection{Formal verification}
\textit{Four-dimensional Kakeya sets}: The pinned catalogue lists no Lean formalization for this result.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{Every Four-Dimensional Kakeya Set Has Full Hausdorff Dimension}, 2026-09-24; citation key \texttt{OAI:Every-four-dimensional-Kakeya-set-has-full-Hausdorff-dimension-September-24-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Every-four-dimensional-Kakeya-set-has-full-Hausdorff-dimension-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Every-four-dimensional-Kakeya-set-has-full-Hausdorff-dimension-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Every-four-dimensional-Kakeya-set-has-full-Hausdorff-dimension-September-24-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Every-four-dimensional-Kakeya-set-has-full-Hausdorff-dimension-September-24-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Every-four-dimensional-Kakeya-set-has-full-Hausdorff-dimension-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex\#L8}{thm:main}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
